window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-672d2fa6d068ad1e"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"audit-dependency-incidents\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">审查依赖项安全事件</h1> <p>将公开的软件包公告转化为安全的代码库审查计划。</p> <p>让 Codex 将公开的软件包或供应链公告转化为只读审查，再检查依赖清单、锁定文件、CI 工作流和脚本，全程不运行不可信代码。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>正在响应公开软件包公告或供应链安全公告的工程与安全团队。</li> <li>在更改依赖项之前，需要检查锁定文件、脚本、CI 权限和缓存的维护者。</li> <li>希望 Codex 收集证据，但不安装软件包或运行不可信代码的事件审查。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">github</a></td> <td>检查代码库文件、拉取请求、工作流和与安全相关的历史记录。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>制定事件审查方案</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请帮我审查此代码库是否受以下公开软件包公告影响：[advisory URL]。\n\n除非我明确批准修复步骤，否则请保持只读。\n\n首先总结：\n\n- 受影响的软件包及版本范围\n\n- 权威来源与更广泛的报道之间的区别\n\n- 哪些证据可以证明此代码库受到影响\n\n- 哪些证据可以排除影响\n\n然后检查：\n\n- 软件包清单和锁定文件\n\n- CI 工作流及其权限\n\n- 安装、构建和 postinstall 脚本\n\n- 如有相关性，检查供应的制品、容器或生成的捆绑包\n\n- 如果公告涉及 CI 或发布，检查缓存或 token 可能暴露的途径\n\n请返回：\n\n- 证据状态：已确认受影响、需要验证或已排除\n\n- 严重程度和影响范围说明\n\n- 支持每项代码库相关结论的文件引用\n\n- 注意事项和建议的后续步骤\n\n除非我明确批准，否则不要安装软件包、运行生命周期脚本、构建项目、执行不可信代码、轮换凭据或清理文件。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d5a186b7366ebd04\">Codex Security</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Agent 审批与安全</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-04f6dcc4a4fe6044\">Codex 网络安全使用规范</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-with-a-safe-audit-plan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">从安全的审查计划开始</h2> <p>依赖项或供应链安全事件进展迅速时，最有用的第一步不是仓促打补丁，而是制定清晰的审查计划：哪些内容发生了变化、哪些软件包或工作流可能受影响，以及需要哪些证据才能确认代码库是否暴露在风险中。</p> <p>在安装、构建、测试或运行任何内容之前，先让 Codex 把公告转成保守的只读检查清单。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-the-first-pass-read-only\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">首轮审查保持只读</h2> <ol> <li>将公开公告、事件报告或受影响软件包清单提供给 Codex。</li> <li>要求它区分权威来源与更广泛的评论或报道。</li> <li>让它说明哪些证据可以证明或排除代码库受影响。</li> <li>让它检查软件包清单、锁定文件、CI 工作流、脚本和相关代码库文件。</li> <li>要求按证据状态、严重程度和建议的下一步归类发现项。</li> </ol> <p>对于软件包安全事件，在弄清公告的影响范围之前，不要运行安装、构建、测试、导入或生命周期命令。Codex 可以搜索锁定文件和工作流，而不必执行不可信代码。</p> <p><a id=\"report-evidence-status-separately-from-severity\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">分开报告证据状态和严重程度</h2> <p>有用的审查结果应分别说明问题的潜在危害有多大，以及证据有多充分：</p> <p><strong>已确认受影响：</strong>锁定文件中存在一个受影响版本的软件包，而且它位于生产依赖路径中。</p> <p><strong>需要验证：</strong>一个 CI 作业具有发布权限，但工作流看起来并未直接安装受影响的软件包。</p> <p><strong>已排除：</strong>软件包名称只出现在文档中，并未出现在软件包清单或锁定文件中。</p> <p><strong>下一步：</strong>在执行任何可能造成破坏的操作之前，先审查拟议的依赖项更新和 token 轮换计划。</p> <p>完成只读审查后，你可以让 Codex 准备修复拉取请求、更新 CI 权限或撰写后续事件记录。请将这些操作与初始审查分开。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn the confirmed findings from this audit into a remediation plan.\n\nFor each finding, include:\n\n- proposed change\n- files or settings to update\n- test or verification step\n- rollback plan\n- whether I need to rotate a credential or review an external system\n\nDo not make changes yet. Keep any command that could execute untrusted code out of the plan unless you explain why it is safe.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请将这次审计中已确认的发现整理成整改计划。\n\n对于每项发现，包括：\n\n- 建议的变更\n- 需要更新的文件或设置\n- 测试或验证步骤\n- 回滚计划\n- 我是否需要轮换凭据或检查外部系统\n\n暂时不要实施变更。任何可能执行不可信代码的命令，都不要纳入计划，除非你解释了它为什么是安全的。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"audit-dependency-incidents\">Audit dependency incidents</h1> <p>Turn a public package advisory into a safe repo-audit plan.</p> <p>Use Codex to turn a public package or supply chain advisory into a read-only audit, then inspect manifests, lock files, CI workflows, and scripts without running untrusted code.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Engineering and security teams responding to public package or supply chain advisories.</li> <li>Maintainers who need to check lock files, scripts, CI permissions, and caches before changing dependencies.</li> <li>Incident reviews where Codex should gather evidence without installing packages or running untrusted code.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">github</a></td> <td>Inspect repository files, pull requests, workflows, and security-relevant history.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build the Incident Audit</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me audit this repository for exposure to this public package advisory: [advisory URL].\n\nStay read-only unless I explicitly approve a remediation step.\n\nFirst, summarize:\n- affected packages and version ranges\n- authoritative sources versus broader reports\n- what evidence would prove exposure in this repo\n- what evidence would rule it out\n\nThen inspect:\n- package manifests and lock files\n- CI workflows and permissions\n- install, build, and postinstall scripts\n- vendored artifacts, containers, or generated bundles if relevant\n- cache or token exposure paths if the advisory involves CI or publishing\n\nReturn:\n- evidence status: confirmed exposure, needs verification, or ruled out\n- severity and blast-radius notes\n- file references for every repo-specific claim\n- caveats and recommended next steps\n\nDo not install packages, run lifecycle scripts, build the project, execute untrusted code, rotate credentials, or clean up files unless I explicitly approve that step.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d5a186b7366ebd04\">Codex Security</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Agent approvals and security</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-04f6dcc4a4fe6044\">Codex cyber safety</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"start-with-a-safe-audit-plan\">Start with a safe audit plan</h2> <p>When a dependency or supply chain incident moves quickly, the first useful output isn't a rushed patch. It's a clear audit plan: what changed, which packages or workflows might be affected, and what evidence would prove exposure in your repo.</p> <p>Use Codex to turn the advisory into a conservative, read-only checklist before installing, building, testing, or running anything.</p> <h2 id=\"keep-the-first-pass-read-only\">Keep the first pass read-only</h2> <ol> <li>Give Codex the public advisory, incident report, or affected package list.</li> <li>Ask it to separate authoritative sources from broader commentary.</li> <li>Have it define evidence that would prove or rule out exposure.</li> <li>Let it inspect manifests, lock files, CI workflows, scripts, and relevant repo files.</li> <li>Ask for findings grouped by evidence status, severity, and recommended next step.</li> </ol> <p>For package incidents, avoid running install, build, test, import, or lifecycle commands until you know what the advisory affects. Codex can search lock files and workflows without executing untrusted code.</p> <h2 id=\"report-evidence-status-separately-from-severity\">Report evidence status separately from severity</h2> <p>A useful audit result should show both how bad a finding would be and how strong the evidence is:</p> <p><strong>Confirmed exposure:</strong> the lockfile contains an affected package version in a production dependency path.</p> <pre><code>**Needs verification:** one CI job has publish permissions, but\nthe workflow does not appear to install the affected package directly.\n\n\n\n\n**Ruled out:** the package name appears in docs only and is not\npresent in manifests or lock files.\n\n\n\n\n**Next step:** review the proposed dependency update and token\nrotation plan before any destructive action.\n</code></pre> <p>Once the read-only pass is complete, you can ask Codex to prepare a remediation PR, update CI permissions, or write a follow-up incident note. Keep those actions separate from the initial audit.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn the confirmed findings from this audit into a remediation plan.\n\nFor each finding, include:\n\n- proposed change\n- files or settings to update\n- test or verification step\n- rollback plan\n- whether I need to rotate a credential or review an external system\n\nDo not make changes yet. Keep any command that could execute untrusted code out of the plan unless you explain why it is safe.\n</code></pre>"};
